{
  "name": "bb_shingle_house",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "bonebight",
  "notes": "A two-storey cedar-shingle house, 7.5 m by 5 m with 3 m storeys under a steep silver-shingle gable roof patched with red, on a 0.75 m bone-block footing. Front faces local -Z with a 1.25 m by 2.5 m open door up a bone-block step; inside are a plank floor, a stair along the back wall to the upper floor, a partition with a doorway on each floor, small-paned windows and an iron stove with a stovepipe through the roof. Carves its interior.",
